              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marsha Owens"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe, but a letter writing campain would be great I will help, I love these cookies and my 88 year old father loves them tooo.",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-09T12:37:09.033Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tigz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The best mincemeat cookie there is. This is more or less the original NoneSuch Mincemeat Prize cookies. (only difference is the original called for 3 1/4 cups sifted flour - which would equal out to 3 cups non-sifted as in this recipe). Unfortunately, it is becoming harder and harder to find the NoneSuch condensed 9oz brick of mincemeat. (time for a letter writing campaign I guess) substituting the jar mincemeat just doesn't come out very well.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-20T11:55:10.213Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda G"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My grandmother used to make a cookie at Christmastime that I just loved. As I grew older I asked her for the recipe, but she said it was a family recipe and when I got married she would give me the recipe. Time went by and I never did get the recipe. Fast forward; I saw this box of Nun-such dried fruit with a cookie recipe on the side. It looked interesting so I made them. And behold - my grandmothers recipe. I make these cookies every Christmas season and it brings back memories of grandma and the wonderful family traditions that we have today. I love this recipe all the more, because it’s getting harder to find the box of mincemeat to make them.",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-24T10:13:36.057Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Laurie Nelson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My Nana's been making these since I was a little girl and they're great! Love them with a cup of tea or coffee. Nice change from the usual sweet cookie. Don't let the mincemeat scare you!",
            "datePublished": "2007-02-14T09:05:18.740Z"
          }
